// Refused: same root cause as ut_note (../why/note.id) -- ut_named calls
// ut_why(name), which traps on a negative utvia index unless `name` is
// already marked in utname (ut_add, ../mark/), and this also needs a real
// case index (casenode/casestart/tline) from case_fixture's chain to report
// through. No fixture combines the two, and the lane's free function slots
// are already spent (see ut_note's note for the accounting).
//
// A setup, a check or a function value a case names runs in the harness as
// surely as the function under test does.
ut_named(int ci, string lead, string name) {
  string ut_why_v = ut_why(name);
  case_err(ci, lead + name + "', which " + ut_why_v);
} return void;
given ut_host_seeded {
  given case_fixture (0, "'given' names '", "port_byte"):() then prints:("fixture.id:4: error: 'given' names 'port_byte', which cannot be tested on the build host (x86_64-unknown-none): it is asm 'in8'\n")
  given case_fixture (0, "'calls' names '", "caller"):() then prints:("fixture.id:4: error: 'calls' names 'caller', which cannot be tested on the build host (x86_64-unknown-none): it calls 'port_byte', which reaches asm 'in8'\n")
}
